\"people who\"","biography subject or topic","biography award category"]},{"id":"character_driven","score":0.36,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"life of\"","catalog text contains \"people who\""]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Rudyard Kipling","confidence":0.9}],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"Kipling’s life and public role traced the British Empire’s shift from apogee to decline, transforming him from imperial apostle to a prophet warning against national downfall.","confidence":0.62},"academicOrientation":{"score":35,"confidence":0.55},"profileConfidence":0.76,"model":"gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"0beb45ec9bc564ac2a67065854b8f9add402e102fba9df7f24aef1f42bbb2895","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"summary":"\"Rudyard Kipling was a unique figure in British history, a great writer and a great imperial icon. He won the Nobel Prize for Literature, he added more phrases to the language than any man since Shakespeare, yet he was also the Apostle of the British Empire, a man who incarnated an era for millions of people who did not normally read poetry.\". \"A child of the Victorian age of imperial self-confidence, Kipling lived to see the rise of Hitler threaten his country's existence. The laureate of the Empire at its apogee, he foresaw that its demise would soon follow his death. His great poem 'Recessional' celebrated Queen Victoria's Diamond Jubilee in 1897; his last poems warned of the dangers of Nazism. The trajectory of his life matched the trajectory of the British Empire from its zenith to its final decades. He himself was transformed from the apostle of success to the prophet of national decline, a Cassandra warning of dangers that successive governments refused to face.\". \"Previous works on Kipling have focused on his writing and on his domestic life. This is the first book to study his public role, his influence on the way Britons saw both themselves and their Empire.","subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Contributions in politics","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-long-recessional-the-imperial-life-of-rudyard-kipling-david-gilmour"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"English Authors","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-long-recessional-the-imperial-life-of-rudyard-kipling-david-gilmour"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Imperialism in literature","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-long-recessional-the-imperial-life-of-rudyard-kipling-david-gilmour"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Colonies","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-long-recessional-the-imperial-life-of-rudyard-kipling-david-gilmour"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Authors, English","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-long-recessional-the-imperial-life-of-rudyard-kipling-david-gilmour"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-long-recessional-the-imperial-life-of-rudyard-kipling-david-gilmour"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"History","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-long-recessional-the-imperial-life-of-rudyard-kipling-david-gilmour"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Et les relations internationales","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-long-recessional-the-imperial-life-of-rudyard-kipling-david-gilmour"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biografie","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-long-recessional-the-imperial-life-of-rudyard-kipling-david-gilmour"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biographies","sourceId":"source-open-library-